# Entity Basics

## Description
Entities are the core business objects of the application. They represent the fundamental business concepts and rules that are essential to the application's purpose. In a clean architecture perspective, entities:

- Express business logic and rules
- Serve as the Single Source of Truth (SSOT) for the entire project
- Are independent of any specific framework or technology
- Remain unchanged regardless of changes in the application's infrastructure or delivery mechanism

## File Organization
- Each entity should have its own file named after the entity (e.g., `Todo.ts`, `Pane.ts`)
- Place all entity files in `demo/src/core/entity/`
- One entity per file, unless types are closely related
- Use proper type references between entities

Example:
```typescript
// Memo.ts
import { RichTextContent } from "./RichTextContent";

type Memo = {
  readonly id: ID["MEMO"];
  content: RichTextContent;  // Using proper type reference
  readonly createdAt: Timestamp;
};
```

- Place utility types (e.g., `Timestamp`) in separate files

Example:
```typescript
// _utility.ts
type Timestamp = number;
export type { Timestamp };

// Memo.ts
import { Timestamp } from "./_utility";
```

## Imports
- Only import from:
  - `../constant/` directory for constants
  - Other files within the `./entity` directory
- Use relative paths for imports (they will be the shortest path)
- Example:
  ```typescript
  import { ID } from "../constant/ID";
  import { Todo } from "./Todo";
  ```

## Entity Structure
- Entity files should ONLY contain type definitions and their exports
- No functions, classes, or other code should be included
- Types should be defined at the top of the file
- Use descriptive type names that match the entity name

## Type Exports
- Export all types at the bottom of the file
- Only export types that are used by other entities
- Internal types (like base types) should not be exported
- Example:
  ```typescript
  // Internal type - not exported
  type BaseUser = {
    id: ID["USER"];
    name: string;
  };

  // External types - exported
  type AdminUser = BaseUser & {
    role: "admin";
    permissions: string[];
  };

  type RegularUser = BaseUser & {
    role: "user";
    preferences: Record<string, unknown>;
  };

  export type { AdminUser, RegularUser };
  ```

